.DS_Store
.playwright-mcp/
node_modules/
*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Rendered images are a build artefact of a build artefact: generated from the
# compiled SVGs, and regenerated whole on every refresh. They were 74% of the
# pack while being 28% of the bytes, because PNG does not delta-compress the way
# SVG does. Portrayal gitignores *.png for the same reason. The DCIM bundle
# renders its own in the browser, so nothing depends on these being committed -
# with ONE exception, below.
assets/exports/**/*.png

# THE HERO'S LEFT-HAND SIDE. site/hero-reveal.js puts the raster we ship to a
# DCIM beside the compiled SVG of the same drawing, and the whole front page is
# that comparison. The rule above excluded it, so the front page was missing
# half of itself in every fresh checkout - and on the deployed site, if the
# deploy is a checkout - while working for anyone who had just run the exporter
# and had it sitting untracked in their tree. Found by check-browser.py running
# on a clean clone, which is the only place the difference shows.
#
# 296 KB against the 283 MB the rule is there to keep out. One file, named
# exactly, so the rule still holds for the other 1605.
!assets/exports/netbox/elevation-images/UfiSpace/ufispace-s9600-72xc.front.png

# Reference photographs for compare.html. Vendor material - copyrighted product
# shots, licensed CAD renders - which is why Portrayal gitignores **/reference/
# too. The page is a local check that a drawing matches the real thing; it says
# where to put them and does nothing until you do.
reference/

# Third-party OFL fonts for the brand generators; brand/fetch-fonts.sh pulls them.
brand/fonts/

# Local lab scenes — a real room, real rack names, not this repo's business.
lab/

# Brainstorming companion mockups (superpowers)
.superpowers/

# The deployed folder, built by tools/build-public.py from tracked files.
/public/
.wrangler/
